note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note gpu/nvidia/checks/nmmq.om: the walk of the matmul() block of CUDApp tests/api_attn_rest_diff.c. mm_init and
note mm_next (gpu/nvidia/om/api/) step the host matmul oracle of src/omega_gpu_matmul_api.c over the elements of C;
note the pending C oracle (CUDAPP_MIGRATION_PENDING_C_MATMUL_ORACLE_GUARD) walks for i < m, for j < n, reading
note c[i*n + j], m*k values of a and k*n of b. Rows:
note   Q m k n GO AN BN VISITS
note                  mm_init on q = {0, 0, k, n, m, 0, 0, 0} must answer GO (1 when there is an element) and set
note                  q[6] = AN and q[7] = BN; then each mm_next step must stand on the next (i, j) of VISITS (2 bytes
note                  each as 4 hex digits, - when none) with q[5] = i*n + j, and answer false after the last.
note Both units carry om2, which a composed program has once, first: check nmmi takes mm_init.om as its head and
note nmm-next.om for mm_next, check nmmn mm_next.om and nmm-init.om. A walk over 4096 elements is refused (ckbad).
text t_name "NMMQ"
fn cname to void
for i ulong len t_name bound 64
ckoc ulong get t_name i
end
end
note value v (2 bytes) of the VISITS field
fn nqv v ulong to ulong
ret or shl ckhex 7 mul v 2 8 ckhex 7 add mul v 2 1
end
note 1 when b, else 0
fn nqb b bool to ulong
if b
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
fn crow to bool
q = new ulong 8 0
if or or ne cklen 0 1 ne ckch 0 0 81 ne ckcnt 8
ckbad
end
put q 4 cknum 1
put q 2 cknum 2
put q 3 cknum 3
if or gt get q 4 4096 gt get q 3 4096
ckbad
end
e = mul get q 4 get q 3
if or gt e 4096 ne ckhexn 7 mul 4 e
ckbad
end
g = nqb mm_init q
if or ne g cknum 4 ne get q 6 cknum 5
ret false
end
if ne get q 7 cknum 6
ret false
end
for v ulong e bound 4096
if eq g 0
ret false
end
if or ne get q 0 nqv mul v 2 ne get q 1 nqv add mul v 2 1
ret false
end
if ne get q 5 add mul get q 0 get q 3 get q 1
ret false
end
g = nqb mm_next q
end
ret eq g 0
end
